1-26T01:54:28.663422561+01:00\",\"level\":\"warning\",\"subject\":\"Sign-in from a new device\",\"message\":\"Account admin signed in from a new device (10.0.2.2, method password)\",\"kind\":\"security\",\"action\":\"review\",\"link\":\"/users\"}],\"read\":0,\"unread\":6}\n"},"GET /api/docker/updates":{"status":200,"body":"{\"running\":false,\"containers\":[],\"stacks\":{},\"available\":0}\n"},"GET /api/security/advisor":{"status":200,"body":"{\"time\":\"2026-11-26T02:03:49.881910884+01:00\",\"score\":30,\"items\":[{\"id\":\"admin-2fa\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"title\":\"Administrators without two-factor authentication: admin\",\"detail\":\"A stolen or guessed password is enough to take over the NAS. Each administrator should turn on two-factor authentication or add a passkey from the account menu (top right).\",\"link\":\"/system/settings#settings-2fa\"},{\"id\":\"backup-none\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"title\":\"No backup task\",\"detail\":\"RAID and snapshots do not protect against theft, fire, ransomware or a mistake on the whole NAS. Back up to another disk, another NAS or the cloud.\",\"link\":\"/backup\"},{\"id\":\"security-updates\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"title\":\"Automatic security updates are off\",\"detail\":\"Debian publishes security fixes several times a month. The fix installs them automatically in the maintenance window (3 AM by default), with a restore point first.\",\"fix\":\"security-updates\",\"link\":\"/system/updates\"},{\"id\":\"guard\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"title\":\"Address blocking is off\",\"detail\":\"Without it, an attacker can try passwords endlessly. The fix blocks an address for an hour after 5 failed sign-ins in 10 minutes, never the local network.\",\"fix\":\"guard\",\"link\":\"/system/guard\"},{\"id\":\"notify\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"title\":\"No notification channel\",\"detail\":\"Nobody is told when a disk fails or a backup stops. Set up e-mail, Telegram, ntfy or the mobile app in Settings.\",\"link\":\"/system/settings\"},{\"id\":\"system-updates\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"title\":\"4 system update(s) waiting\",\"detail\":\"Install them from Updates, or let the maintenance window do it.\",\"link\":\"/system/updates\"},{\"id\":\"system-disk\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"title\":\"The system disk has no redundancy\",\"detail\":\"If it fails, the NAS no longer starts until the system is reinstalled (the data volumes are not affected). Mirror it onto a second disk, or at least keep a system backup and a configuration export (Storage → Disks → System disk).\",\"link\":\"/storage/disks#system-disk\"}]}\n"},"GET /api/system/info":{"status":200,"body":"{\"hostname\":\"strata-vm\",\"os\":\"Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie)\",\"kernel\":\"6.12.118+deb13-amd64\",\"arch\":\"amd64\",\"cpuModel\":\"AMD Ryzen 5 5625U with Radeon Graphics\",\"cores\":4,\"memTotal\":4111757312,\"swapTotal\":0,\"swapFree\":0,\"uptime\":869.22,\"bootTime\":\"2026-11-26T01:50:24.128783449+01:00\",\"load\":[0.25,0.2,0.17],\"timezone\":\"Europe/Paris\",\"temps\":[],\"version\":\"0.15.4\",\"vendor\":\"QEMU\",\"product\":\"Standard PC (Q35 + ICH9, 2009)\",\"rootTotal\":20922114048,\"rootFree\":17875623936}\n"},"GET /api/system/stats":{"status":200,"body":"{\"cores\":[2.5252525252525304,1.5075376884422065,1.980198019801982,2.0000000000000018],\"history\":[{\"t\":1795654776523,\"cpu\":3.1289111389236512,\"memUsed\":581996544,\"memTotal\":4111757312,\"netRx\":0,\"netTx\":0,\"diskRead\":0,\"diskWrite\":176064.44601692128},{\"t\":1795654778524,\"cpu\":0.12515644555695093,\"memUsed\":581996544,\"memTotal\":4111757312,\"netRx\":0,\"netTx\":0,\"diskRead\":0,\"diskWrite\":0},{\"t\":1795654780523,\"cpu\":0.3750000000000031,\"memUsed\":581996544,\"memTotal\":4111757312,\"netRx\":0,\"netTx\":0,\"diskRead\":0,\"diskWrite\":227345.5705160901},{\"t\":1795654782523,\"cpu\":0.3754693366708417,\"memUsed\":581971968,\"memTotal\":4111757312,\"netRx\":0,\"netTx\":0,\"diskRead\":0,\"diskWrite\":0},{\"t\":1795654784525,\"cpu\":0.12499999999999734,\"memUse